# DevMind Conventions

## Runtime: Bun (not Node)
- Use `bun`, `bun add`, `bun run`, `bun --watch`, `bunx` everywhere
- Never suggest `node`, `ts-node`, `tsx`, `nodemon`, `npm install`, `npx`

## Monorepo
- Three apps: `apps/api` (Express :8080), `apps/worker` (BullMQ), `apps/ui` (Next.js :3000)
- One shared types package: `packages/shared` (@devmind/shared) — no runtime logic, types only
- Docker is for infra only: Postgres+pgvector, Redis Stack, RedisInsight

## Phase Boundaries (do not add early)
- No Dockerfiles for apps until Phase 6
- No BullMQ consumers or queue logic until Phase 2
- No LangGraph / agent code until Phase 4
- No dashboard pages or SSE until Phase 5

## GitHub MCP — STRICTLY READ-ONLY
The `user-github` MCP namespace must never be used for writes.
Forbidden: create_repository, push_files, create_pull_request, merge_pull_request,
create_issue, add_issue_comment, create_branch, create_webhook, and any other mutating tool.

## Database
- Use the `postgres` npm package (postgresjs) for Postgres — not `pg`
- Use `ioredis` for Redis
- Schema lives in `apps/api/src/db/schema.sql` — auto-applied by docker-compose on first boot

## TypeScript
- `"moduleResolution": "bundler"` in all tsconfigs (Bun native)
- `"target": "ESNext"`, `"module": "ESNext"`
- `strict: true` always on
